  "cards": [
    {"dot": "cyan", "title": "The backend decides", "items": [
      "A toggle sends the state it asks for and waits; only a state command turns it (app.js 74–77, 176–179). A lamp that does not switch stays off on the screen.",
      "the home keeps the lights and the scene in flow context; a scene or all off changes several tiles in one state command (examples/switch.json 29–31)."]},
    {"dot": "amber", "title": "Kept for the next phone", "items": [
      "command() keeps each state and its label before sending it (core.py 173–182); send_profile() hands them to every phone that says hello (core.py 148–152). A profile command empties them (core.py 162–166).",
      "Node-RED also gets a status event with the states when it connects (nodered.py 28–30)."]}
  ]
